<title>ITALY: Aeroporti di Roma trading temporarily halted.</title>
<headline>Aeroporti di Roma trading temporarily halted.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>- Shares in newly listed Aeroporti di Roma were temporarily suspended after they were quoted 31 percent higher than their offer price in pre-trading, a spokeswoman for the stock exchange council said.</p>
<p>Shares in the airport management company were quoted at 14,450 lire, up from an offer price of 11,000 lire.</p>
<p>A fresh attempt to start matching offers and bids will be made at 1040 (0840 GMT) and, if successful, trading will get underway at 1050 (0850 GMT).</p>
<p>Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
</text>
